{"id": "EUVD-2026-96917", "enisaUuid": "09220277-2905-39e8-ac62-646a2b539793", "description": "JupyterHub through 6.0.1 contains an identifier collision vulnerability that allows authenticated users to overwrite another user's named-server OAuth client by registering a hyphenated username. Attackers holding a name like alice-prod can overwrite the client for alice's server prod, breaking OAuth login and revoking tokens by stopping their own server.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T17:00:17", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/jupyterhub-oauth-client-id-cross-user-collision", "https://github.com/jupyterhub/jupyterhub/blob/3e516c6f382b481e815ec455befb2f14d80d337b/jupyterhub/user.py#L563-L567", "https://github.com/jupyterhub/jupyterhub/blob/3e516c6f382b481e815ec455befb2f14d80d337b/jupyterhub/oauth/provider.py#L719-L754", "https://github.com/jupyterhub/jupyterhub/blob/3e516c6f382b481e815ec455befb2f14d80d337b/jupyterhub/user.py#L1174-L1186", "https://github.com/jupyterhub/jupyterhub", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jupyterhub-through-6.0.1-oauth-client-id-collision-via-unescaped-hyphen"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108752", "GHSA-h63v-vvgj-vrfh"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b36c4daf-4789-39a7-9cb9-3c18e3e874d5", "product": {"name": "jupyterhub", "vendor": {"name": "jupyterhub"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e67e3a0b-cae2-36e8-a1b4-324dd919760d", "vendor": {"name": "jupyterhub"}}], "isExploited": false}